        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1380">

                <pb facs="0918" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg802"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/221.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Spanish Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I beg to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your note of April 9, in regard to the expulsion of Spanish
                    subjects from Torreon, and in reply to inform you that the Department is in
                    receipt of a telegram from its representative at El Paso, Texas, dated April 9,
                    in which it is stated that General Venustiano Carranza undoubtedly gave to the
                    press the statement attributed to him in yesterday’s newspapers to the effect
                    that the property of Spaniards expelled from Torreon would not be
                    confiscated.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
